Z||000000||mbramble||09-16-2001||03:22 PM||||Just got my project car to a stage where I can drive it around in the neighborhood.  Took it down the road the other day and after about 3 miles the engine just died.  Pulled over to the side and tried to start it but it would just turn over and not start.  Sat about 3 minutes and it started right up and came home.  I have let this thing idle for long periods of time to recharge the battery as I have worked on it and it has never shut off.  Drove it 4 miles yesterday, no problem.  Just took it out and got maybe 1/4 mile and it shut off.  Sat for a couple minutes and it started right up.  Did this a couple times. <P>Any ideas on where to begin to look??  The car has been off the road for a year or more but I have let the engine run regularly over several months as I worked on the interior/exterior.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rogue_Ant||09-16-2001||03:29 PM||||First Check basic things next time it dies, I.E. spark, fuel pressure, ect.<BR>It sounds like its heat related, possible your coil gets hot and the wiring seperates then when it cools down, it works again.<P>Rogue||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||09-16-2001||03:38 PM||||If it's heat related, why can I let it idle forever with no problem???  <P>What is the easiest way to check for fuel on these 2.8's??  I have only driven a 4 cyl up till now and you just pop the cover off the breather and have a look.....<P>Thanks much.||||reg||1
